ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
 for i,(q,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((q,[options[i]]+options[:i]+options[i+1:],e))
family(['Report the firearm\'s loss or theft','Report the licence document\'s loss or theft','Report the location of unlawful possession','Notify a change in application information'],[
('An owner discovers that a firearm has been stolen, but the licence card is still safely at home. Which reporting duty directly applies to the missing item?','Section120(11) requires reporting the firearm\'s theft within24hours after awareness to the nearest police station to where it occurred.'),
('A wallet containing the licence card is stolen, but the licensed firearm remains secure. Which report is required even though no firearm is missing?','Section29 requires the holder to notify the Registrar of the licence document\'s loss or theft within24hours of discovery.'),
('A person becomes aware of ammunition that is not in anyone\'s lawful possession and knows where it is. Which reporting duty applies?','Section120(2) requires reporting the location to a police official without delay. It does not authorise taking possession.'),
('Information supplied in an approved application changes, without any loss or theft. Which general duty requires the Registrar to receive updated information?','Section26 requires written notification of changed application information within30days.')])
family(['Within24hours of becoming aware','Within7days of the request','Within30days of the change','Without delay'],[
('A person who controlled a firearm learns that it was destroyed. Under section120(11), when must the destruction be reported?','Loss, theft and destruction all trigger reporting within24hours after the person becomes aware.'),
('An owner is not carrying a firearm when an identified authorised official makes a general section106request to produce it for inspection. What period does that section allow?','Subject to section107, section106 requires production within seven days. The carrying-with-you provision is different.'),
('A licence holder\'s physical address changes. What period applies to the holder\'s written notification under section25?','Written notification must be given within30days of the change; it is not deferred until renewal.'),
('A person knows the location of a firearm that is not in lawful possession. What urgency does section120(2)require for reporting the location to police?','The statutory wording is without delay, rather than the separate24-hour rule for reporting loss or theft of a controlled firearm.')])
family(['Negligent injury or property damage','Reckless or endangering handling','Failure to take precautions around a loaded firearm','Handling while under the influence'],[
('Careless firearm use causes damage to another person\'s property. Which section120(3)offence description most directly fits the resulting harm?','Section120(3)(a) addresses injury or property damage caused by negligent use.'),
('A person handles a firearm with reckless disregard for nearby people, although nobody is injured. Which section120(3)prohibition can apply without actual injury?','Section120(3)(b) prohibits handling likely to endanger safety or property, or with reckless disregard for them.'),
('A person controls a loaded firearm in circumstances creating a risk but takes no reasonable precautions to avoid the danger. Which section120(3)failure is described?','Section120(3)(c) specifically addresses failure to take reasonable precautions in a risky loaded-firearm situation.'),
('A person handles a firearm after becoming affected by an intoxicating substance. Which independent section120prohibition is most directly relevant?','Section120(4) prohibits handling while under the influence of a substance with an intoxicating or narcotic effect.')])
family(['Knowingly false application information','Unauthorised alteration of a document','Use of another person\'s document','A false entry in a required register'],[
('An applicant knowingly gives an incorrect answer in a firearm licence application to conceal a relevant fact. Which documentary offence is directly described?','Section120(9)(f) prohibits knowingly false, incorrect or misleading application information.'),
('A licence holder changes a printed detail on the card without the Registrar\'s permission. Which documentary offence is directly described?','Unauthorised additions, alterations or erasures on competency or licensing documents are prohibited.'),
('A buyer presents a relative\'s licence as though it authorises the buyer to acquire possession. Which documentary offence is directly described?','Section120(9)(e) prohibits using another person\'s document to procure possession.'),
('A person deliberately records a fictitious transaction in a register required under the Act. Which documentary offence is directly described?','Section120(9)(g) prohibits a false entry in a required register.')])
family(['Pointing without good reason','Discharge in a public place without good reason','Giving control to an impaired person','Supplying an unauthorised recipient'],[
('As a joke and without good reason, a person points an imitation that is likely to be believed to be a firearm at someone. Which prohibition is directly relevant?','Section120(6) includes objects likely to be believed to be firearms; a joke does not automatically provide good reason.'),
('A person fires a firearm in a built-up public place without good reason. Which offence description directly applies to the location and conduct?','Section120(7) prohibits discharge in a built-up area or public place without good reason.'),
('An owner gives a firearm to someone the owner knows is under the influence of an intoxicating substance. Which separate prohibition concerns the transfer of control?','Section120(5) prohibits giving control to a person known, or reasonably expected to be known, to be under the influence.'),
('A seller hands a firearm to a buyer who has no lawful authority to possess it and no applicable exception. Which supply offence is directly involved?','Section120(10)(a) prohibits giving possession to someone who is not allowed under the Act to possess it.')])
family(['The existing authorities cease to be valid','Surrender is required within24hours','An appeal does not suspend unfitness','Disposal must follow the statutory process'],[
('A final section102declaration of unfitness is made. What happens from that date to the person\'s competency certificates, licences, permits and authorisations?','Section104(1) makes the authorities cease to be valid from the relevant declaration or conviction date.'),
('A person has just become unfit under the Act and still holds the documents, firearms and ammunition covered by section104. What immediate compliance deadline applies?','Section104(2) requires surrender to the nearest police station within24hours.'),
('A person declared unfit has filed an appeal and asks whether the filing alone restores possession rights. Which rule answers that question?','Unfitness remains in effect pending finalisation of the appeal under section104(1)(b).'),
('After surrender following unfitness, the former owner wants to sell the firearms. What restriction governs the next step?','Section104 requires disposal through a dealer or as the Registrar determines, within the applicable period; surrender does not authorise private handover.')])
family(['All relevant competency and licensing documents','All firearms in the person\'s possession','All ammunition in the person\'s possession','The nearest police station'],[
('A person complying with section104hands over all firearms and ammunition but keeps the competency certificate and licence cards. What required category has been omitted?','The surrender duty includes all competency certificates, licences, permits and authorisations issued to the person under the Act.'),
('A person declared unfit surrenders documents and ammunition but retains an ordinary firearm merely because it was not involved in the incident. What has been omitted?','The duty covers all firearms in the person\'s possession, not only one involved in the event.'),
('A person declared unfit surrenders every firearm and document but keeps remaining cartridges. Which required category has been omitted?','Section104(2) also requires surrender of all ammunition in the person\'s possession.'),
('A person asks where the section104surrender of documents, firearms and ammunition must be made. Which destination does the Act specify?','Section104 specifies the nearest police station, rather than an informal private recipient.')])
family(['Produce the authority when requested','Identify yourself forthwith','Produce the firearm for inspection','Require the official\'s identification and authority'],[
('An identified authorised official stops a person who is carrying a firearm and requests the licence for that firearm. Which section107duty applies to the document?','A person carrying a firearm must produce its licence, permit or authorisation for inspection on request; the general seven-day provision is not a substitute.'),
('During a lawful section107check, the official asks the carrier to establish personal identity. Which duty addresses that request?','The person must identify themselves forthwith to the satisfaction of the official.'),
('The carrier has produced the licence, but the authorised official also requests inspection of the firearm. What further section107duty applies?','The person must also produce the firearm for inspection when requested under section107.'),
('Someone claims section107inspection powers but has not identified themselves or shown an appointment certificate or authorisation. Which reciprocal safeguard does the Act require?','The official exercising these powers must identify themselves and produce the appointment certificate or authorisation.')])
family(['Confirm the decision','Vary the decision','Reverse the decision','Condone a late appeal on good cause'],[
('After considering a lawful appeal, the Appeal Board leaves the challenged decision unchanged. Which statutory outcome is this?','Section133 permits the Board to confirm a decision.'),
('The Appeal Board modifies part of a challenged decision while retaining the rest. Which statutory power describes this?','Section133 permits the Board to vary the decision, rather than only accept or reject it wholesale.'),
('The Appeal Board overturns the challenged refusal. Which statutory outcome is described?','Reversing a decision is one of the powers listed in section133.'),
('An appeal notice arrives after the ordinary period, with a substantiated explanation why timely submission was impossible. Which procedural power may the Board exercise under regulation91?','The Board may condone late submission on good cause; lateness is not automatically excused merely because an appeal is desired.')])
family(['Possession under section117','Failure to report under section118','Failure to take reasonable steps under section119','Direct evidence of the reported event'],[
('In a possession prosecution, the State invokes the carefully qualified statutory inference concerning a firearm found on specified premises after reasonable efforts to link it to another person. Which provision is concerned?','Section117 concerns evidential presumptions of possession. Its conditions and the possibility of contrary evidence raising reasonable doubt matter.'),
('In a failure-to-report prosecution, an authorised possessor has not produced the allegedly missing firearm within seven days of a police request, and no contrary evidence raises reasonable doubt. Which evidential provision addresses this?','Section118 provides the specified inference relating to loss, theft or destruction and failure to report; it is not an irrebuttable rule.'),
('A charge concerns failure to take reasonable steps to prevent unlawful firearms being brought onto controlled premises. Which statutory presumption specifically addresses that duty?','Section119 addresses failure to take reasonable steps, subject to its evidential qualifications.'),
('A witness personally observed the theft and describes what happened, rather than asking the court to infer it solely from non-production. What kind of evidence is described?','First-hand testimony describes the event directly. It is distinct from invoking a statutory presumption, though its reliability must still be assessed.')])
family(['Written proof that the report was made','An official reference number','The nearest station to the incident location','The time the person became aware'],[
('A person reports in person the location of a firearm not lawfully possessed under section120(2). What acknowledgement must the police official provide immediately?','For such a report, section120(2)(b) requires written proof that the report was made, with a reference number used for telephonic or similar reports.'),
('A person makes the section120(2)report by telephone. What acknowledgement does the Act specify for that type of report?','For a telephonic or similar report, the official must provide the official reference number.'),
('A firearm is stolen while its owner is visiting another town. Under section120(11), which police station is identified for the report, rather than simply the station near the owner\'s home?','The statute specifies the police station nearest to the place where the loss, theft or destruction occurred.'),
('A firearm theft occurred overnight, but its lawful possessor discovers it the following morning. What event starts the section120(11)reporting period?','The24-hour period runs from becoming aware of the loss, theft or destruction, not from an unknown time of occurrence.')])
family(['Obtain appropriate authority to keep it','Arrange lawful deactivation','Dispose of it in terms of the Act','Seek temporary authority for disposal'],[
('An heir wants an inherited ordinary firearm as a usable possession of their own. Which section148route must be followed before relying on that ownership?','The heir must apply for the appropriate licence, permit or authorisation; inheritance is not a possession licence.'),
('An heir does not want an inherited firearm to remain a functioning firearm and chooses the lawful deactivation alternative. Which section148option reflects that choice?','Section148 allows deactivation in accordance with the Act. This is a regulated process, not permission for improvised alteration.'),
('An heir does not wish to retain an inherited firearm and chooses a lawful transfer rather than deactivation. Which statutory option applies?','The firearm must be disposed of in terms of the Act, so the recipient and transfer route must be lawful.'),
('An heir needs a reasonable period to arrange lawful disposal and seeks a time-limited permission under section148(2). Which route is relevant?','The Registrar may issue section21temporary authorisation to allow an heir reasonable time to dispose of the firearm.')])
family(['Carrying into the declared zone','Storing within the declared zone','Allowing prohibited presence in the zone','Seizure of an unlawfully present firearm'],[
('A person with no applicable authorisation enters a formally declared firearm-free zone carrying a firearm. Which section140restriction is directly breached?','A normal licence does not override the prohibition on carrying firearms or ammunition into a declared zone without applicable authorisation.'),
('A person with no applicable authorisation keeps ammunition in a locker inside a formally declared firearm-free zone. Which section140restriction directly concerns this arrangement?','Section140 prohibits storage of firearms or ammunition in the zone without the applicable authorisation.'),
('A person permits firearms to be present in a formally declared firearm-free zone despite having no applicable authority to do so. Which section140restriction is directly relevant?','The section separately prohibits allowing firearms or ammunition to be in the zone without applicable authorisation.'),
('A police official lawfully finds a firearm in a declared firearm-free zone in contravention of the notice. Which section140power concerns taking that firearm into custody?','Section140 permits seizure of firearms or ammunition present in contravention of the zone notice, subject to the statutory conditions.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==52
